{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788222063,"nonce":"HauKOCjQKajxn3lS4RDA4hgGCqg=","message":"WHAT THE FIXES CHANGED — the second half of the record, completing comment #3.\nMerged to main in `51f39bc`; assembly at `172e168`.\n\n**The one real defect: a partial mutation was reported as `bad-args`.**\n`VerbRegistry.Execute` maps `VerbArgsException` to `{ok:false, code:\"bad-args\"}`\nwith no sign that anything changed, and both verbs threw AFTER writing.\n`bill-add` ran `AddBill` and THEN `Configure`, so any bad config argument left\nthe bill in the stack — an agent reads `bad-args`, retries, and now has two bills.\n`storage-set` threw inside its per-target loop after writing `copy_from` and\n`priority`, so `Act()` was never reached and there was NO JOURNAL ROW AT ALL: an\nunprovenanced state change, which is exactly what `Stamp`/`NoAction` exist to\nprevent, and a violation of 4087644's journal rule. Both now validate every\nargument BEFORE the first write (`ValidateBillArgs`, `ValidateStorageArgs`).\n\n**`RecipeGate` now asks `Worker.AvailableReport` rather than `AvailableOnNow`.**\nSame call — `RecipeWorker.AvailableReport`'s base body is `return AvailableOnNow(...)`\n— but an override supplies a real reason string, and 3.4's `surgery-options`\nalready did it this way. The two halves of one codebase no longer disagree about\nwhich member to ask the same question.\n\n**The collapsed `ideo-or-faction` gate now names its `MemeDef`**, the way the\nresearch gate already named its `ResearchProjectDef.LabelCap`.\n\n**`AddWarnings`' mechanitor early-return moved inside its `!any` guard.** Vanilla\nfalls through to the skill test when a mechanitor IS present, so the branch was\nreporting nothing for a recipe no colonist could actually reach.\n\n**`PawnsFinder.AllMaps_FreeColonists` is snapshotted rather than iterated live** —\nit clears and refills a STATIC list (Class E), and it was new uncatalogued surface.\n\n**The acceptance suite that did not exist now does:** `accept/3.6-bills-storage.py`,\n1171 lines, phase 0 a shape contract on a `has_key` predicate DISTINCT from\n`eq(..., None)`. Its dry-run refuses to claim a pass — it reports that it printed\nN expectations and asserted none of them. That wording was right and has since\nbeen adopted by all five drivers in `accept/` (`61e3fc1`).\n\n## STILL OWED, and it is the only thing standing between this and closed\n\n**THE SUITE HAS NEVER RUN.** 119 expectations, all of them unexecuted code. Per\nthis round's standing rule, treat \"119 checks written\" as ZERO evidence until a\nlive run. The verbs compile and ship in `172e168` — the first assembly that has\never contained them, since this branch sat unbuilt on the other machine — but\nnothing here is proven. This issue does NOT close until that run is green.","files":null}]}